@participant4 Could you share links to what exactly the VSCode team did to take care of this? I searched recent pull requests for `apparmor`, `profile`, and `wayland`, but I couldn't find anything relevant.

The only thing is a comment talking about changing `code.desktop` https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/212430#issuecomment-2109960783 but as far as I understand it's about forcing Wayland + adding some extra flags rather than manually adding some kind of profile?

Edit: This is how we solved this in our app thanks to the information in this issue: https://github.com/gravitational/teleport/pull/43595

> @participant4 Could you share links to what exactly the VSCode team did to take care of this? I searched recent pull requests for `apparmor`, `profile`, and `wayland`, but I couldn't find anything relevant.

@participant5 simple answer. vscode did nothing. ubuntu did. ubuntu has vscode (among some other popular 3rd party apps) as part of their `apparmor` profiles https://packages.ubuntu.com/noble/amd64/apparmor/filelist
Maybe the author of those changes (@participant19 John Johansen <<email-scrubbed>> https://gitlab.com/jjohansen) can share

@participant14 

I asked the question about the pre-release tag in https://github.com/electron-userland/electron-builder/pull/8808#issuecomment-2618896028.

It is being used to mean that 26.x is ready for production, but not yet widely adopted. Personally, I prefer to hang back and wait until there is a release labeled as `latest`, but it will depend on your situation whether you want to move to 26.x already.
